# Loan Classification

## 📌 Description

This project is an end-to-end **Machine Learning classification project** developed to predict loan outcomes based on various financial, employment, demographic, and credit-related attributes of loan applicants.

The project focuses on building a structured and reusable machine learning workflow rather than simply training a model. Different types of features are handled using appropriate preprocessing techniques, including **missing-value imputation, feature scaling, one-hot encoding, and ordinal encoding**. These transformations are organized using Scikit-learn's `Pipeline` and `ColumnTransformer`.

Two different machine learning algorithms are implemented and evaluated:

* **Support Vector Machine (SVM)** — a supervised learning algorithm that finds an optimal decision boundary between classes.
* **Random Forest Classifier** — an ensemble learning algorithm that combines multiple decision trees to improve classification performance.

To improve the models, **RandomizedSearchCV** is used for hyperparameter tuning. Cross-validation is also applied to obtain a more reliable estimate of model performance across different data splits.

The models are evaluated using several classification metrics, including **Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC**. Using multiple metrics provides a broader understanding of how well the models perform rather than relying only on accuracy.

### 🎯 Project Objective

The main objective of this project is to understand and implement a complete machine learning classification workflow, from **raw data preprocessing to model training, hyperparameter optimization, cross-validation, and final model evaluation**.

